Z||000000||contra||08-19-2000||10:17 AM||||I think i want to try and put flush headlights in my fiero with maybe clear lexan covers, and some of those blue fake HID light bulbs. I was just wondering if anybody else has done this to their car. i'm aware of kits you can buy, but i think i'd rather try and make it myself just to save me some money. If anybody can give me any insight or instructions that'd be great.<BR>thanx<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-19-2000||10:59 AM||||I agree that some of the flush mounted headlight kits are expensive, however...Tom (a long standing member of this forum) sells a nice kit for about $170US.  Not cheap, but not really expensive compared to some of the others I've seen.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||08-19-2000||03:00 PM||||I've been looking around, trying to see what production cars have lights that will fit.<P>New Grand prix lights might fit but you have to cut the lens off the front to get the angle right. It should still work fine since the lenses don't diffuse the light. Another that might work is Chrysler Concord headlights if you want an inset style, but you still have to cut the turn signals off.<P>I don't know if it'll be cheaper but It would give it a different look than the kits out there already.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||08-20-2000||09:31 AM||||I have seen Tom's headlight kit in his web site, i think it is prety cool and dosen't cost too much, But has any one seen it with a lexan cover? ir is it hard to add one?||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||08-20-2000||01:10 PM||||Covers aren't legal in allot of places. Other, bigger, problem is that a cover can screw up the light patern. <P>I think Tom's kit used DOT legal lights but it's still not legal every place. Some areas don't allow any type of modification to lighting even if the lamping is DOT legal. You might want to check that so you don't have inspection problems or make youself a ticket magnet.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||08-20-2000||05:54 PM||||I personally think that this is idea is ugly, but shouldnt sunfire lights fit in there pretty easy?<P><BR>I like how the lights like toms look when they are round!!||||reg||1
